{"version":2,"width":120,"height":30,"timestamp":1791990288,"title":"Claude Code 2.1.300: a follow-up typed while a dimmed next-prompt suggestion shows in the input box","env":{"TERM":"xterm-256color"},"pm":{"agent":"claude","agent_version":"2.1.300","initial_status":"running","bug":"VERIFY-R11 #1 (regression from typing-permit): after a turn Claude draws a faint (SGR 2) suggestion of the next prompt (`❯ commit this`) in the input box. Readiness read it as typed text, so every follow-up parked on screen_not_ready (\"the input box already holds text\") and ended PROMPT_NOT_SUBMITTED. Fixed by TuiProfile::input_screen (Claude: tui/claude/screen.rs::without_suggestion).","source":["Live run 2026-10-14 23:04 in D:/pm-scratch-r12/trust-cap: run_agent \"Create a file named hello.txt ... then reply done\", then a follow-up. Claude launched with CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_PROMPT_SUGGESTION=1 so the suggestion is always generated.","Flight recording of the pane (GET /panes/{id}/flight), D:/pm-night/r12/evidence/r12live-flightB.json. Output events are kept up to the suggestion (9.23 s). The reactions are the bytes Claude really wrote when the follow-up was typed (11.05 s) and submitted (11.17 s)."]}}
